From 62eba8633b55ad335ab621a3ac5bd851777f5e54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 09:47:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] mm: fix sharded i_mmap read-side walkers

Dynamic i_mmap sharding moves VMAs out of the central mapping->i_mmap tree after write-side contention.  Readers that continue to walk the central tree directly can then miss every VMA for a sharded regular-file mapping.

Add a common sharded-aware read walker and convert the regular-file read-side users that can observe sharded state, including rmap, DAX writeback, memory failure collection, khugepaged page-table retract, and pagewalk.  Keep unconverted special mapping classes on the central tree by excluding shmem and hugetlbfs from dynamic shard installation.

Also close the unmap_mapping_range() install race by rechecking shard state after taking the central read lock, and make vma_link_file() validate that callers pass shard-lock storage as a pair.

Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
